This product bundles third-party code, each under its own licence, with the
licence text committed beside the code it covers:

  public/vendor/headtts/                     HeadTTS, MIT
  public/vendor/transformers/
    transformers.min.js                      transformers.js, Apache-2.0
    ort-wasm-simd-threaded.asyncify.*        ONNX Runtime Web, MIT
  public/vendor/inter/                       Inter, SIL Open Font License 1.1
  public/dictionaries/en-us.txt              CMU Pronouncing Dictionary,
                                             simplified BSD, via HeadTTS
  src/supertonic/helper.js                   Supertonic's browser helper, MIT
  onnxruntime-web (bundled into the          ONNX Runtime Web, MIT; licence text
    offscreen page by the build)             in public/vendor/transformers/

The build copies src/supertonic/LICENSE into the package as vendor/supertonic/.

Supertonic 3's model weights are not bundled. They are downloaded from Hugging
Face when the user presses Download in Settings, after agreeing to their
licence, the BigScience Open RAIL-M License (dated August 18, 2022). Its text
is src/supertonic/MODEL_LICENSE.txt, shipped in the package as
vendor/supertonic/MODEL_LICENSE.txt.

What was checked in each case, and the one package that failed the check, is in
public/vendor/NOTICE.md. That file is the record, not this one.

Kokoro's model weights and voices (Apache-2.0, onnx-community/Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX
and its timestamped sibling) are NOT bundled. They are downloaded from the setup
page when the user asks for them, from URLs pinned in src/weights.js, and
verified against SHA-256 digests baked into the build before use.
